The waiter stands behind the counter.
He looks at me.
"Good afternoon, what would you like?" he asks kindly.
I answer politely.
"Good afternoon," I say.
"I would like a large coffee, please."
The waiter nods.
"Very gladly," he says.
"Would you also like to eat something?"
I point at the delicious cakes.
"Yes, could I please have a piece of chocolate cake?" I ask.
The waiter smiles.
"Of course," he answers.
"Just take a seat," he then says.
"I will bring everything to your table."
That is a very nice service.
"Thank you very much," I say.
